@startuml pr-close-test-gaps-after
!include ../../theme.iuml
title pr-close-test-gaps — with teamscale-mcp (ts_agent_helper replaced)

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
autonumber

actor "Developer" as Dev

box "Developer workstation" $ws_bg
    participant "Claude\n(pr-close-test-gaps skill)" as Agent
    participant "git\n(local)" as Git
end box

box "Teamscale server" $ts_bg
    participant "teamscale-mcp\n(central sidecar)" as MCP
    participant "Teamscale\nREST API" as TS
end box

Dev -> Agent : /teamscale:pr-close-test-gaps

group Agent resolves the PR (was inside ts_agent_helper)
    Agent -> Git : git branch --show-current
    Git --> Agent : <branch>
    Agent -[$tool_color,bold]> MCP : <size:15>**tool getMergeRequests(project, filter=<branch>, status=OPEN)**</size>
    MCP -> TS : GET /api/projects/{p}/merge-requests
    TS --> MCP : open merge requests
    MCP --> Agent : open merge requests
    Agent -> Agent : pick exact sourceBranch match → MR id
    opt no matching MR
        Agent -> Git : git symbolic-ref origin/HEAD
        Git --> Agent : <base branch>
    end
end

Agent -[$tool_color,bold]> MCP : <size:15>**tool getTestGaps(project, baseline, end, merge-request-mode)**</size>\nX-Teamscale-User + X-Teamscale-Token
activate MCP
MCP -> TS : GET /api/projects/{p}/test-gaps.csv\nAuthorization: Basic base64(user:token)
activate TS
TS --> MCP : test-gap data\n(uniform path, method, lines, test state)
deactivate TS
MCP --> Agent : test gaps (tool result)
deactivate MCP

Agent -> Agent : pick gaps to close;\ndetect test framework from existing tests
Agent -> Agent : write tests, run them to confirm they pass
Agent --> Dev : summary — gaps closed / skipped

note over Agent, TS
  The agent performs the PR resolution ts_agent_helper bundled.
  Requires the Test Gap Analysis + Merge Requests tags in the tool surface.
  Gaps still recompute server-side from CI coverage after tests are pushed.
end note

@enduml
